BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:DJ Ahmet
DTSTART:20250525T180000Z
DTEND:20250525T195000Z
DTSTAMP:20250525T180000Z
UID:kEWEJetcCZ
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 97 mins (1h37m)\n\nFifteen-year-old shepherd Ahmet r
 ebels against his conservative North Macedonian farming village when he ge
 ts a taste of electronic dance music in this heartwarming dramedy\, winner
  of the World Cinema – Audience Award Prize at Sundance 2025. Sponsored 
 by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/dj-ahmet
LOCATION:AMC Pacific Place 11\, 600 Pine Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tales From the Magic Garden
DTSTART:20250525T180000Z
DTEND:20250525T192500Z
DTSTAMP:20250525T180000Z
UID:sMLREA0LXf
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 71 mins (1h11m)\n\nIn this stop motion marvel from t
 he Czech Republic based on the stories of author Arnošt Goldflam (“The 
 Zookeeper’s Wife”)\, three young children visit their late grandmother
 ’s house\, where they take turns spinning fantastical tales to better un
 derstand loss\, compassion\, and empathy. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.sif
 f.net/festival/tales-from-the-magic-garden
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Coexistence\, My Ass!
DTSTART:20250525T183000Z
DTEND:20250525T201500Z
DTSTAMP:20250525T183000Z
UID:r4xdmGyaYM
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 95 mins (1h35m)\n\nComedy about Israel and Palestine
  is a high-wire act and perhaps never more so than now\, which is part of 
 what makes this documentary about Israeli comedian Noam Shuster-Eliassi so
  riveting. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/coexistence-my-a
 ss
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Crowd
DTSTART:20250525T190000Z
DTEND:20250525T202000Z
DTSTAMP:20250525T190000Z
UID:vnnNnQaEeH
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 70 mins (1h10m)\n\nA story of a group of friends com
 ing together to plan a farewell party\, The Crowd is also a vibrant portra
 it of a younger generation in Iran\, determined to live life on their own 
 terms. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/the-crowd
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Familiar Touch
DTSTART:20250525T200000Z
DTEND:20250525T214500Z
DTSTAMP:20250525T200000Z
UID:SrHdMDV3jo
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 91 mins (1h31m)\n\nRuth Goldman (Broadway legend Kat
 hleen Chalfant) has been living with dementia for some time\, and the time
  has come to place her in an assisted living facility. But while this may 
 seem like the end\, for her it represents something like a new beginning i
 n this poignant\, Venice Film Festival-winning drama. Sponsored by:\n\nhtt
 ps://www.siff.net/festival/familiar-touch
LOCATION:Shoreline CC Theater\, 16101 Greenwood Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Paul Anka: His Way
DTSTART:20250525T200000Z
DTEND:20250525T215000Z
DTSTAMP:20250525T200000Z
UID:g0IX1j6Mhv
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 99 mins (1h39m)\n\nHe faced it all\, stood tall\, an
 d did it his way. Get the inside scoop on the life and career of Paul Anka
 \, the Canadian-born son of immigrants who rocketed to the top of the char
 ts not just as a teen heartthrob\, but as the songwriter of some of Americ
 a’s greatest standards. Director John Maggio scheduled to attend May 23 
 screening. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/paul-anka-his-wa
 y
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Between Goodbyes
DTSTART:20250525T203000Z
DTEND:20250525T222000Z
DTSTAMP:20250525T203000Z
UID:BfCVhcQcLe
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 96 mins (1h36m)\n\nA Dutch adoptee and her Korean bi
 rth parents try to build familial bonds across languages and cultural diff
 erences from halfway around the world in this tear-jerking\, decades-spann
 ing documentary from debut filmmaker Jota Mun. Director Jota Mun scheduled
  to attend. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/between-goodbye
 s\n\nFilm is also being streamed.
LOCATION:AMC Pacific Place 11\, 600 Pine Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sons
DTSTART:20250525T204500Z
DTEND:20250525T223500Z
DTSTAMP:20250525T204500Z
UID:3jQv1kswqM
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 99 mins (1h39m)\n\nWriter/director Gustav Möller (S
 IFF 2018’s The Guilty) returns to the Fest with another pulse-pounding a
 nd morally gray thriller\, as a prison guard learns that a young man from 
 her past has just been transferred to her post.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/fe
 stival/sons
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Chef & The Daruma
DTSTART:20250525T210000Z
DTEND:20250525T224000Z
DTSTAMP:20250525T210000Z
UID:kdX9ZsjG9h
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 90 mins (1h30m)\n\nSeattle loves its sushi\, but did
  you know the cuisine’s North American popularity is thanks to a man nam
 ed Hidekazu Tojo? Learn the story of the chef who changed the world after 
 moving from Japan to Vancouver in the 1970s\, staying true to his traditio
 ns despite all odds. Director Mads Baekkevold\, producer Matthew Dix\, and
  subject Chef Hidekazu Tojo scheduled to attend. Lovers of Japanese food a
 nd baked goods won't want to miss our trivia giveaway of gift cards to Sai
 nt Bread and The Wayland Mill at the May 25 screening! Sponsored by:\n\nht
 tps://www.siff.net/festival/the-chef-and-the-daruma
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Color Book
DTSTART:20250525T213000Z
DTEND:20250525T232000Z
DTSTAMP:20250525T213000Z
UID:6tF2nRZYtF
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 98 mins (1h38m)\n\nFilmmaker David Fortune won the D
 irectors to Watch Award at the 2025 Palm Springs International Film Festiv
 al for this black and white debut sensation\, about a recently widowed Bla
 ck father who just wants to take his young disabled son to his first profe
 ssional baseball game. Director David Fortune and producer Kristen Uno sch
 eduled to attend. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/color-boo
 k\n\nFilm is also being streamed.
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Little Red Sweet
DTSTART:20250525T223000Z
DTEND:20250526T001500Z
DTSTAMP:20250525T223000Z
UID:Kcau59LDXo
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 92 mins (1h32m)\n\nIn a rapidly changing Kowloon Cit
 y\, one Hong Kong family struggles to keep their traditional dessert shop 
 open in the face of illness\, generational desires\, and gentrification in
  Vincent Chow Wing’s wistful\, nostalgic family drama.\n\nhttps://www.si
 ff.net/festival/little-red-sweet
LOCATION:Shoreline CC Theater\, 16101 Greenwood Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Slanted
DTSTART:20250525T223000Z
DTEND:20250526T002500Z
DTSTAMP:20250525T223000Z
UID:SWLL7JjnNO
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 104 mins (1h44m)\n\nChinese American teen Joan Huang
  just wants to fit in at her high school\, but when she hastily undergoes 
 an experimental medical procedure to become Caucasian\, the consequences c
 ould be devastating in this biting speculative fiction satire. SXSW Grand 
 Jury winner. Director Amy Wang scheduled to attend.\n\nhttps://www.siff.ne
 t/festival/slanted
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Boong
DTSTART:20250525T230000Z
DTEND:20250526T004500Z
DTSTAMP:20250525T230000Z
UID:2LV02YnZ1Q
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 93 mins (1h33m)\n\nWhen nine-year-old schoolboy Boon
 g hears a rumor that his father has passed\, he and his best friend Raju m
 ake the journey to Moreh to investigate in this class-conscious\, charming
  coming-of-age border drama from debut filmmaker Lakshmipriya Devi. Sponso
 red by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/boong\n\nFilm is also being strea
 med.
LOCATION:AMC Pacific Place 11\, 600 Pine Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:U Are the Universe
DTSTART:20250525T231500Z
DTEND:20250526T011000Z
DTSTAMP:20250525T231500Z
UID:AiC5jAeFZx
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 101 mins (1h41m)\n\nIn this Ukraine-shot tale of fin
 ding connection under the most devastating and isolating of circumstances\
 , a space trucker thinks he’s the last living person in the universe…u
 ntil a call from a distant space station sets him on a course across the c
 osmos. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/u-are-the-universe
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cloud
DTSTART:20250525T233000Z
DTEND:20250526T014500Z
DTSTAMP:20250525T233000Z
UID:OBG72ksGwU
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 124 mins (2h04m)\n\nLegendary filmmaker Kiyoshi Kuro
 sawa (Pulse\, Cure\, Tokyo Sonata) ramps up the thrills in this genre-bend
 ing potboiler about a craven opportunist who finds success as an internet 
 reseller\, only for revenge-seeking vigilantes to come calling. Love Akira
  Kurosawa almost as much as Kiyoshi Kurosawa? Come prepared May 19 for a t
 rivia giveaway of tickets to Ran\, returning in 4K to SIFF Cinema Downtown
  from May 30–June 4! Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/clou
 d
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Know Her Name
DTSTART:20250526T000000Z
DTEND:20250526T013000Z
DTSTAMP:20250526T000000Z
UID:yk3YjxQlla
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 80 mins (1h20m)\n\nIn this amazing slice of film her
 story\, learn the legacy of women directors who have fought to be seen and
  heard and have their films preserved…and how to not let the next genera
 tion get lost in the same inequitable and homogenized system. Producer He
 idi Lasi scheduled to attend. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festi
 val/know-her-name\n\nFilm is also being streamed.
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Shepherds
DTSTART:20250526T010000Z
DTEND:20250526T030500Z
DTSTAMP:20250526T010000Z
UID:FQl5n43p4W
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 113 mins (1h53m)\n\nIn this layered\, bucolic drama 
 from Francophone director Sophie Deraspe (Antigone) full of moments of bea
 uty and harsh reality\, a Quebeçois marketing executive gives it all up a
 nd moves to the French Alps to become a sheep herder. Sponsored by:\n\nhtt
 ps://www.siff.net/festival/shepherds\n\nFilm is also being streamed.
LOCATION:Shoreline CC Theater\, 16101 Greenwood Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Rebuilding
DTSTART:20250526T013000Z
DTEND:20250526T031500Z
DTSTAMP:20250526T013000Z
UID:bN6DnQKdrt
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 95 mins (1h35m)\n\nIn Max Walker-Silverman’s tende
 r follow-up to A Love Song (SIFF 2022 Golden Space Needle Award for Best 
 Performance)\, Josh O’Connor (Challengers) stars as a Coloradan cowboy w
 ho reconnects with his daughter and ex-wife after a wildfire takes his fam
 ily ranch.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/rebuilding
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Wailing
DTSTART:20250526T013000Z
DTEND:20250526T033000Z
DTSTAMP:20250526T013000Z
UID:EM2cn1ygYn
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 107 mins (1h47m)\n\nThree women separated in time an
 d space are unknowingly connected by a threat that nobody can explain. Som
 ething is stalking them and provoking unthinkable acts of violence with on
 e eerie thing in common: the disturbing sound of a wailing. Sponsored by:\
 n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/the-wailing
LOCATION:AMC Pacific Place 11\, 600 Pine Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Diamonds
DTSTART:20250526T020000Z
DTEND:20250526T042500Z
DTSTAMP:20250526T020000Z
UID:nHUZTxFPbJ
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 135 mins (2h15m)\n\nIn this lush\, metatheatrical cr
 owdpleaser that was a box office smash in its native Italy\, SIFF favorite
  Ferzan Özpetek gathers 18 of his country’s greatest actresses to tell 
 the story of a Rome-based tailoring shop that makes costumes for the big s
 creen. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/diamonds
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Twinless
DTSTART:20250526T021500Z
DTEND:20250526T040500Z
DTSTAMP:20250526T021500Z
UID:Ehq0cT1VhE
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 100 mins (1h40m)\n\nIn this Portland-set dark comedy
  from James Sweeney (2019’s crowdpleasing Straight Up)\, two men (Dylan 
 O’Brien and Sweeney) trauma-bond at a support group for people who have 
 lost their twin. Winner of the Sundance 2025 US Dramatic Audience Award. D
 irector James Sweeney scheduled to attend.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festiv
 al/twinless
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Good Boy
DTSTART:20250526T023000Z
DTEND:20250526T035500Z
DTSTAMP:20250526T023000Z
UID:kkpWJ6b3QF
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 73 mins (1h13m)\n\nYou know when you think your dog 
 is staring at nothing? Turns out they’re really looking for ghosts! In t
 his supernatural chiller\, Indy (the goodest boy of all!) is all that stan
 ds between his human best friend and the dark forces that haunt their rura
 l family home. Sponsored by:\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festival/good-boy
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
